# Dependencies
/node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.js

# A plugin writer's lock beside a document, held for one write (M27 U6) — and,
# beside it, what a hook told each session and what the status line last read (M51 U6)
*.emd.lock
*.emd.told
*.emd.status
*.emd.status.refreshing
*.emd.*.tmp

# Build output
/dist
/out-tsc
/tmp

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Editors
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Obsidian. docs/ is a vault; its settings, pane layout and open tabs are one
# editor's state, not the spec. Leading `**/`, because a pattern containing a
# slash anchors to the directory this file sits in, and the vault is `docs/`.
**/.obsidian/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit real financial data.
# Real statement files and database files stay local. Public tests use only
# the synthetic fixtures in fixtures/synthetic/. See docs/conventions.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/fixtures/real/
*.emd
# ...except this project's own memory, which is the M22 dogfood (D-240). It holds
# decisions, units, review entries and open questions and no financial data at
# all, so the rule above does not apply to it. Every write beside it leaves a
# timestamped `.bak` (the plugin's own protection) and those are not the document.
!/docs/memory.emd
*.emd.*.bak
# The old extension stays ignored: real documents named before D-156 are still
# on the machine, and this list exists to keep them out of the repo.
*.emerald
*.sqlite
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
!fixtures/synthetic/**/*.csv
!fixtures/synthetic/**/*.xlsx
!fixtures/synthetic/**/*.xls

# The demo (M33 U1): built, and its document made at build time, never committed.
/dist-demo
/.demo

# The desktop shell (M9). Built, not committed, like the other outputs.
/dist-electron

# The installers (M9). `build/` is the opposite — icons are build *inputs*, cut
# from src/ui/emerald.svg by `npm run icons`, and they are committed so a fresh
# clone can package without a separate step. Only the script's own report is not.
/release
build/icons.log

# The Claude plugin's MCP server (M7). Built, not committed, like the other two outputs.
/dist-plugin
# Its desktop extension's contents, staged by scripts/mcpb.mjs before it packs release/emerald.mcpb (M42 F9)
/dist-mcpb

# The MCP App page, built by `vite build --mode frame` and embedded in the plugin (M41 U1)
/.frame
# The frame drawn without a host (`npm run frame:try`): a page holding a copy of whatever document it was run on
/.frame-try

# The long-form record of closed milestones, kept in the maintainer's checkout and
# not in the repository (D-495). scripts/archive-decisions.mjs still writes it.
/docs/archive/
